      "type": "Talk",
      "properties": {
        "abstract": "Paul Phillips will talk about collections for Scala.\n\n\"Based on my extensive experience with scala collections, I'm writing my own. The focus is much tighter: immutable, performant, predictable, correct. The talk will alternate between why the scala collections manage none of those things, and how I hope to do better.\"\n\nPaul Phillips is a co-founder of Typesafe and the most prolific committer to Scala.\n\nLocation: LinkedIn\n\nSchedule:\n\n6:30-7:00 - networking\n\n7:00-7:10 - announcements etc\n\n7:10-~8:40 - talk\n\n8:40-9:00 - networking",
